    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d663">

                <pb facs="0714" n="626" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg626"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.3827/1</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)<anchor n="16"
                        xml:id="d663-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 61</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-06-07">June 7, 1933</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>:</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>The Governments of Nicaragua and the Dominican Republic have concurred in the
                    interpretation of the Habana Convention on Commercial Aviation given in this
                    instruction. The governments of other countries parties to this Convention have
                    not yet made definite replies.</p>
                <p>For your information, it may be stated that this Government does not contemplate
                    entering into formal agreements with the countries parties to the Habana
                    Convention supplementing the Convention itself. This Government merely desires
                    to reach an understanding with these countries in regard to the interpretation
                    of the Convention so far as concerns the right of private aircraft of one of the
                    parties to enter territory of the other parties without the necessity of
                    obtaining an authorization for the flight from the government of the country in
                    which the flight is to be made.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Acting Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Francis White</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d663-f1" n="16" type="source" xml:id="d663-f1-content">
                <p>The omitted paragraphs at the beginning of this instruction are the same, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, as instruction No. 150, January
                    27, to the Minister in the Dominican Republic, <ref target="#pg609">p.
                    609</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
